          %h2#Idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            which sends
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
                to their
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebras+of+functions"} algebras of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
                with values in the
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℝ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebras"} algebras
                (instead of, say
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+algebras"} smooth algebras
                aka “
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty
                \-rings”),
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
                between these manifolds to the corresponding
                = succeed "/" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback+of+a+function"} pullback
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/precomposition"} precomposition
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+homomorphisms"} algebra homomorphisms
                between these function algebras
          %p
            turns out to be
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fully+faithful+functor"} fully faithful
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
            embedding of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SmthMfd"} SmthMfd
            into the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alg"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi Alg
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}Alg
          %p
            This is remarkable, because such a relation between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spaces"} spaces
            and their
            %em plain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebras+of+functions"} algebras of functions
            is (more) manifest only for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+varieties"} affine varieties
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+geometry"} algebraic geometry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
            manifestly suggests that they behave to some extent similarly to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+varieties"} affine varieties
            with respect to
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            = succeed ".)" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+between+algebra+and+geometry"} duality between algebra and geometry
          %p
            Related “miracles” in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+geometry"} differential geometry
            = succeed "-nature," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+geometry"} algebro-geometric
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivations+of+smooth+functions+are+vector+fields"}> derivations of smooth functions are vector fields
                ,
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K%C3%A4hler+C%5E%E2%88%9E-differentials+of+smooth+functions+are+differential+1-forms"}> Kähler C^∞-differentials of smooth functions are differential 1-forms
                ,
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+differential+forms+form+the+free+C%5E%E2%88%9E-DGA+on+smooth+functions"} smooth differential forms form the free C^∞-DGA on smooth functions
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+Serre-Swan+theorem"}> finitely generated projective modules over smooth functions are smooth vector bundles
                \.
          %p
            Accordingly, the embedding of smooth manifolds into
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+duality"} formal duals
            of
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+geometry"} algebraic geometry
            into
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+geometry"} differential geometry
            %em without
            strengthening the notion of “algebra” to something like
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+algebras"} smooth algebras
          %p
            This is useful and is used particularly for discussions in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/synthetic+differential+geometry"} synthetic differential geometry
            — cf. e.g. the emphasis on “Weil algebras”, hence of would-be function algebras on
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimally+thickened+points"} infinitesimally thickened points
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#KolarSlovakMichor93"} Kolář, Michor &amp; Slovák 1993 §35
          %h2#statement Statement
          %p
          #MilnorExercise.num_lemma
            %h6 Lemma
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a{:href => "#Pursell52"}> Pursell, Section 8
                , 1952)
              %br/
              For a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi SmthMfd
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in SmthMfd
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/evaluation+map"} evaluation map
              (from its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying"} underlying
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
              to the
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-set"} hom-set
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "left", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mi ev
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi Hom
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi Alg
                                %mi ℝ
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi C
                            %mn ∞
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ,
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi x
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↦
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mo ↦
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{array}{l}
                    X
                    \&amp;\overset{ev}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    Hom_{Alg_{\mathbb{R}}}
                    \\big(
                    C^\infty(X)
                    ,\,
                    \\mathbb{R}
                    \\big)
                    \\\
                    x &amp;\mapsto&amp;
                    \\big(
                    \\phi \,\mapsto\, \phi(x)
                    \\big)
                    \\end{array}
            %p
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijection
          %p
            The statement also appears in
            %a{:href => "#MilnorStasheff74"} Milnor &amp; Stasheff (1974) Prob. 1-C (p. 11)
            and a detailed proof different from the one below is given by
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#KolarSlovakMichor93"} Kolář, Michor &amp; Slovák 1993 Lem. 35.8 &amp; Cor. 35.9
          %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              We provide a simplified proof using
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hadamard%27s+lemma"} Hadamard's lemma
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi M
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi\colon C^\infty(M)\to\mathbf{R}
              is a homomorphism of real algebras.
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi R
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M=\mathbf{R}^n
              for some
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n\ge0
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi y
                        %mi i
                      %mo =
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y_i=\phi(x_i)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi R
                      %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_i\colon\mathbf{R}^n\to\mathbf{R}
              is the
              = succeed "th" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi i
                    %mo −
                    %msub
                      %mi y
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⋅
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo −
                    %msub
                      %mi y
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi(f)=\phi(f(y)+\sum_i (x_i-y_i)\cdot g_i)=f(y)+\sum_i (\phi(x_i)-y_i)\cdot \phi(g_i)=f(y),
            %p
              where the functions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g_i
              are provided by
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hadamard%27s+lemma"} Hadamard's lemma
            %p
              For a general
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whitney%27s+embedding+theorem"} Whitney's embedding theorem
              to embed
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              into some
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi R
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{R}^n
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi R
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M\subset\mathbf{R}^n
              is closed.
            %p Consider the composition
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi R
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi M
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi R
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(\mathbf{R}^n)\to C^\infty(M)\to \mathbf{R},
            %p
              where the first homomorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
              is given by restricting along the embedding. The composition is given by evaluating at some point
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi R
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p\in\mathbf{R}^n
            %p
              If
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo ∉
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p\notin M
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
              that vanishes on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              and does not vanish at
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              constructed by the smooth Tietze extension theorem, or simply use smooth bump functions. The function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
              vanishes on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              and therefore belongs to the kernel of the map
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ρ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo ∉
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p\notin M
              does not vanish on the element
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ρ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p\in M
          %p
            Pursell’s theorem (Lemma
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MilnorExercise"}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo =
                  %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X = \ast
            (the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point+space"} point
          #Embedding.num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "center center center", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi SmthMfd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⟶
                        %mtd
                          %msubsup
                            %mi Alg
                            %mi ℝ
                            %mi op
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↦
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi C
                            %mn ∞
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                            %mrow
                              %msup
                                %mrow
                                %mi f
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} ↑
                          %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                            %mrow
                              %msup
                                %mrow
                                %mrow
                                  %msup
                                    %mi f
                                    %mo *
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi Y
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↦
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi C
                            %mn ∞
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi Y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{array}{ccc}
                    SmthMfd
                    \&amp;\longrightarrow&amp;
                    Alg_{\mathbb{R}}^{op}
                    \\\
                    X &amp;\mapsto&amp; C^\infty(X)
                    \\\
                    \\mathllap{{}^f}\Big\downarrow
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    \\Big\uparrow\mathrlap{{}^{{f^\ast}}}
                    \\\
                    Y
                    \&amp;\mapsto&amp;
                    C^\infty(Y)
                    \\end{array}
            %p
              which sends a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+number"} finite
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimensional
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+topological+space"} paracompact
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/second+countable+topological+space"} second countable
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+dual"} formal dual
              of) its
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebra"} algebra
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≔
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(X) \coloneqq C^\infty(X, \mathbb{R})
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+functor"} full and faithful functor
            %p
              In other words, given a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pair"} pair
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X,Y
              then the operation of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/precomposition"} precomposition
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback+of+a+function"}> pullback of functions
              )
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi g
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^\ast(g) \coloneqq g \circ f
              constitutes a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+bijection"} natural bijection
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "left", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi C
                            %mn ∞
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo ,
                          %mi Y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mo ∼
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi Hom
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi Alg
                                %mi ℝ
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi C
                            %mn ∞
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi Y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ,
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %msup
                            %mi C
                            %mn ∞
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi f
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↦
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi f
                            %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{array}{l}
                    C^\infty(X,Y)
                    \&amp;\overset{\sim}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    Hom_{Alg_{\mathbb{R}}}\big(
                    C^\infty(Y)
                    ,\,
                    C^\infty(X)
                    \\big)
                    \\\
                    f &amp;\mapsto&amp; f^\ast
                    \\end{array}
            %p between
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                          %mo →
                          %mi Y
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to Y
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ℝ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebra"} algebra
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphisms"} homomorphisms
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi C
                            %mn ∞
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ←
                          %msup
                            %mi C
                            %mn ∞
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi Y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(X)\leftarrow C^\infty(Y)
            %p
              In particular, the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphisms"} diffeomorphisms
              between smooth manifolds are in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+bijection"} natural bijection
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphisms"} isomorphisms
              between their
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebras+of+functions"} algebras of functions
          (
          %a{:href => "#KolarSlovakMichor93"}> Kolář, Slovák &amp; Michor 1993 Cor. 35.10
          )
          #ProofFromMilnorExercise.proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              It is clear that the functor is
              = succeed ";" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/faithful+functor"} faithful
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+functor"} full
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\phi
                    \\;\colon\;
                    C^\infty(Y, \mathbb{R})
                    \\longrightarrow
                    C^\infty(X, \mathbb{R})
            %p
              there exists a smooth function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \to Y
              such that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo =
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi = f^\ast
            %p
              To that end, observe that given a point
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/postcomposition"} postcomposition
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
              with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/evaluation+map"} evaluation map
              at
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi ϕ
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ev
                          %mi x
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C^\infty(Y, \mathbb{R})
                    \\overset{ \phi }{\longrightarrow}
                    C^\infty(X, \mathbb{R})
                    \\overset{ ev_x }{\longrightarrow}
                    \\mathbb{R}
            %p
              is an algebra homomorphism of the form assumed in Pursell’s theorem (Lemma
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MilnorExercise"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x) \in Y
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ev
                      %mi x
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi ev
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    ev_x \circ \phi \;=\; ev_{f(x)}
                    \\,.
            %p
              This implies that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
              acts on any
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \in C^\infty(Y)
              by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right center left", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi g
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ↦
                            %mi ϕ
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo ↦
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi g
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo ↦
                          %msub
                            %mi ev
                            %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi g
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo ↦
                          %msub
                            %mi ev
                            %mrow
                              %mi f
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi x
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi g
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo ↦
                          %mi g
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo ↦
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi g
                          %mo ∘
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} )
                          %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                            %mrow
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{array}{rcl}
                    g
                    \&amp;\overset{\phi}{\mapsto}&amp;
                    \\big(
                    x \mapsto \phi(g)(x)
                    \\big)
                    \\\
                    \&amp;=&amp;
                    \\Big(
                    x \mapsto ev_x(\phi(g))
                    \\Big)
                    \\\
                    \&amp;=&amp;
                    \\Big(
                    x \mapsto ev_{f(x)}(g)
                    \\Big)
                    \\\
                    \&amp;=&amp;
                    \\Big(
                    x \mapsto g\big(f(x)\big)
                    \\Big)
                    \\\
                    \&amp;=&amp;
                    \\Big(
                    x \mapsto (g \circ f)(x)
                    \\Big)
                    \\mathrlap{\,,}
                    \\end{array}
            %p
              hence that it acts by precomposition with the assignment
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi g
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi f
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\phi(g) \;=\; g \circ f
                    \\,.
            %p
              It just remains to observe that this
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is necessarily
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
              is given on
              %em all
