          %h2#references References
          %p
            The case of the category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
            with (just)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphisms"} diffeomorphisms
            between them is proved in
          %ul
            %li#Pursell52
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lyle+Eugene+Pursell"}> Lyle Eugene Pursell
              \:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Algebraic structures associated with smooth manifolds
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://www.proquest.com/docview/2327629257"} proquest:2327629257
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/pursell-dissertation.pdf"} pdf
          %p following an announcement in
          %ul
            %li#Shanks51
              M. E. Shanks,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Rings of functions on locally compact spaces
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.ams.org/journals/bull/1951-57-04/S0002-9904-1951-09521-X/S0002-9904-1951-09521-X.pdf"} pdf
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Janez+Mr%C4%8Dun"}> Janez Mrčun
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On isomorphisms of algebras of smooth functions
                %strong 133
                10 (2005) 3109-3113 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0309179"}> arXiv:math/0309179
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1090/s0002-9939-05-07979-7"} doi:10.1090/s0002-9939-05-07979-7
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Janusz+Grabowski"}> Janusz Grabowski
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Isomorphisms of algebras of smooth functions revisited
                %strong 85
                (2005) 190–196 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0310295"}> arXiv:math/0310295
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s00013-005-1268-3"} doi:10.1007/s00013-005-1268-3
          %p The statement for domain a point appears as an exercise in:
          %ul
            %li#MilnorStasheff74
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Milnor"}> John Milnor
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Stasheff"} James Stasheff
              = succeed "," do
                %em Characteristic Classes
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://press.princeton.edu/books/paperback/9780691081229/characteristic-classes-am-76-volume-76"} ISBN:9780691081229
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "/nlab/files/Milnor_exercise.pdf"} pdf
          %p A proof is spelled out in
          %ul
            %li#Dubuc79
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eduardo+Dubuc"}> Eduardo Dubuc
              , Prop. 0.7 in:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Sur les modèles de la géométrie différentielle synthétique
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cahiers"} Cahiers de Topologie et Géométrie Différentielle Catégoriques
              %strong 20
              3 (1979) 231-279 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item?id=CTGDC_1979__20_3_231_0"}> numdam:CTGDC_1979__20_3_231_0
              \&amp;rbrack;
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (in defining the
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cahiers+topos"} Cahiers topos
          %p
            Expository accounts for the case of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphisms"} isomorphisms
            are in
          %ul
            %li#Grabowski78
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Janusz+Grabowski"}> Janusz Grabowski
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Isomorphisms and ideals of the Lie algebras of vector fields
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01406466"} doi:10.1007/BF01406466
            %li#MarsdenRatiuAbraham02
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jerrold+Marsden"}> Jerrold Marsden
                , J. Ratiu, R. Abraham, Theorem 4.2.36 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Manifolds, tensor analysis, and applications
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.springer.com/gp/book/9780387967905"} ISBN:978-1-4612-1029-0
            %li#Grabowski05
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Janusz+Grabowski"}> Janusz Grabowski
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Isomorphisms of algebras of smooth functions revisited
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0310295"} arXiv:math/0310295
          %p The general statement and its proof is discussed in:
          %ul
            %li#KolarSlovakMichor93
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ivan+Kol%C3%A1%C5%99"}> Ivan Kolář
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Michor"} Peter Michor
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jan+Slov%C3%A1k"} Jan Slovák
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Natural+operations+in+differential+geometry"} Natural operations in differential geometry
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.emis.de/monographs/KSM/"} book webpage
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-3-662-02950-3"} doi:10.1007/978-3-662-02950-3
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.emis.de/monographs/KSM/kmsbookh.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Discussion that takes the dual algebraic formulation as the very definition of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
            is in
          %ul
            %li#Nestruev03
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jet+Nestruev"}> Jet Nestruev
              , section 6 of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Smooth manifolds and Observables
              %strong 220
              Springer (2002, 2020) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-030-45650-4"}> doi:10.1007/978-3-030-45650-4
              , ISBN:0-387-95543-7,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://nzdr.ru/data/media/biblio/kolxoz/M/MD/MDdg/Nestruev%20J.%20Smooth%20Manifolds%20and%20Observables%20(ISBN%200387955437)(Springer,%202003)(224s)_MDdg_.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            The analog of the statement for real algebras refined to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+algebras"} smooth algebras
            is Theorem 2.8 in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"}> Ieke Moerdijk
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gonzalo+Reyes"} Gonzalo E. Reyes
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Models+for+Smooth+Infinitesimal+Analysis"} Models for Smooth Infinitesimal Analysis
              Springer (1991)
        .revisedby
